com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L313-L314","doc":"Cardinality of each index set: 4 indices per nucleon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_ladder_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_ladder_shape","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L288-L311","doc":"Both nucleon characters share the unified ladder shape\n`{m, m-2, m-4, m-8}`, with `m_proton = 11`, `m_neutron = 9`.\nThis is established purely by unfolding the closed-form\ndefinitions and the index-set lists — no matrix manipulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_neutron_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_neutron_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L269-L286","doc":"**Theorem (manuscript): closed-form χ_std for neutron.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_proton_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chi_std_proton_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L248-L267","doc":"**Theorem (manuscript chi-std-pernucleon-theorem §Proof):\nclosed-form χ_std for proton braid.**  Verified externally via\nsympy (chi_std_pernucleon_derivation.py). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.neutronBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.neutronBraid","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L172-L180","doc":"Neutron per-nucleon braid word from `neutron_cross`:\n\n- gen 0: five (1, 0) + one (1, -H_A) + one (1, -H_A/2)\n- gen 1: three (1, -H_A) + one (1, -H_A/2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.protonBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.protonBraid","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L162-L170","doc":"Proton per-nucleon braid word from `proton_cross`:\n\n- gen 0: six (1, 0) + one (1, -H_A/2)\n- gen 1: three (1, -H_A) + one (1, -H_A/2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chiStdEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chiStdEval","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L156-L158","doc":"χ_std evaluator: word → scalar via matrix-product trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.evalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.evalWord","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L150-L154","doc":"Evaluate a nucleon braid word by matrix-product of its factor\nmatrices in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.heckeFactorMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.heckeFactorMat","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L142-L148","doc":"Build a 2×2 matrix from a single Hecke factor on a given generator:\n`c · σ + d · I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.NucBraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.NucBraidWord","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L139-L140","doc":"Per-nucleon braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instReprGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instReprGen","kind":"instance","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instReprGen.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instReprGen.repr","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instDecidableEqGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.instDecidableEqGen","kind":"instance","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen.g1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen.g1","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen.g0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen.g0","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.Gen","kind":"inductive","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L135-L137","doc":"Which Hecke generator a factor acts on in H_3(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.d","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.c","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L131-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.HeckeFactor","kind":"structure","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L130-L133","doc":"Hecke factor (c, d) ∈ ℝ² representing `c · σ + d · I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.neutronIndices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.neutronIndices","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L125-L126","doc":"Neutron index set (ladder-shifted by 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.protonIndices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.protonIndices","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L122-L123","doc":"Proton index set (from Laurent-polynomial grouping). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chiStdClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.chiStdClosedForm","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L118-L120","doc":"Core closed-form: `(H_A / 4) · Σ_{k ∈ indices} [k]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.qNum_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.qNum_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket**, unconditional — the local body\ndiffers from `qIntBal` only in writing the negative power as a `zpow`\n(`q ^ (-(k : ℤ))` rather than `q⁻¹ ^ k`), which is `zpow_neg` + `inv_pow`.\n\nThis site was the one the `qou-qint` drain could not reach while the file was\nred on `main`; it is migrated now that the two closed-form theorems above are\nproved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.qNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.qNum","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L102-L104","doc":"q-number `[k]_q := (q^k - q^{-k}) / (q - q⁻¹)` for `k ∈ ℕ, k ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.hoefsmit_σ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.hoefsmit_σ₂","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L94-L98","doc":"σ_2 on std = (2,1): 2×2 mixing block with axial distance ρ = -2.\nOff-diagonal entries carry `√(q⁴+q²+1)/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.hoefsmit_σ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.hoefsmit_σ₁","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L90-L92","doc":"σ_1 on std = (2,1): diagonal `diag(q, -q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.M2.trace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.M2.trace_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-std-pernucleon-closed-form.lean#L82-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.M2.smul_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiStdPerNucleon.M2.smul_eq","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"http